A||N||51||watdge||What's your best kill story?  Does everyone know how you smoked that camaro?  Share!!||||14||
Z||000000||watdge||10-01-2000||10:45 PM||||Hey folks,<BR>Thought I inquire because I don't see much on here about road drags or races.. like on other forums I have visited before.  I know that the folks here do more than listen to people talk about being beaten by a ricey Neon....  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>The young, Mechanical Engineering student,<BR>Jeremy<BR> <IMG SRC="http://venus.spaceports.com/~flagg/pictureforformum.jpg"> ||||reg||14
Z||000001||Cooter||10-01-2000||11:21 PM||||For the most part, this Forum frowns upon the use of public roadways for speed/acceleration competitions. I hope you are not too disappointed.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cheever2||10-01-2000||11:31 PM||||I agree.  We would have even fewer Fieros left if our lead feet get the better of us.  I stopped doing that stuff years ago. <BR> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||watdge||10-01-2000||11:42 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cooter:<BR><B>For the most part, this Forum frowns upon the use of public roadways for speed/acceleration competitions. I hope you are not too disappointed.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Oh I see, I had no idea, but that's perfectly alright with me.  Just wanted to know what had been accomplished, but your points are both well taken.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"><BR>Thanks for pointing that out for me all the same!<P><P>------------------<BR>The young, Mechanical Engineering student,<BR>Jeremy<BR> <IMG SRC="http://venus.spaceports.com/~flagg/pictureforformum.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Carrolles||10-02-2000||12:37 AM||||Although we frown on it doesn't mean we don't like to talk about it and hear stories.<P>Welcome to the Forum.  Where are you studying Engineering? How far along are you?<P>I got my BSME from LSU back in the early 70s.<P>I'd suggest that you take the EIT exam as soon as you feel you have enough courses to give it a try.  I took it for practice when I started Junior year and was surprised that I passed.  I took the FE exam after I completed 6 years working.  My PE license has kept me employed many years when non-registered friends were being layed off.<P>Also I'd suggest setting up an NCEES Record as soon as you are licensed.<P>Good luck,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000005||Sillhouette.com||10-02-2000||03:38 AM||||Well I got a lead foot I guess a couple of them.  Life is too short to worry about carefullness and life insurance and I do race my Fiero both on the Track and on the street.  If the Forum does not like that well I also know of a good psychologist that can help you get over it.  <BR>My lates kill was a 1989 Corvette, Yellow convertible.   It happended on back roads from a beach in the Toronto area about 100 KM away.  I never intended to race the thing I just wanted to come home at a faster pace than anyone else.  The corvette was in front of me and I let him pass other cars I just followed at a good distance.  After a while I got sick of looking at his two round tail lights and when I had a chance I passed him.  While passing him initially I had a very good acceleration.  Latter side by side we kept beside each other well onto 180 KPH (I don't know what that is in MPH but that is the limit my gauge reads)  I don't know if he just played with me or he could not pass me because he was a half car length behind me and stayed there.  When I finally passed him it was over.  After that we got into some light traffic.  I kept passing cars at a normal rate but he could not keep up with me.  I know he tried with some dangerous maneuvers on a two lane road.  I never believed the story that the Fiero was probably cancelled because of direct competition with the Corvette until yesterday.<P>Cheers||||reg||1
Z||000006||Patrick||10-02-2000||03:22 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Life is too short to worry about carefullness...<HR></BLOCKQUOTE> Unfortunately, it's not just your <I>own</I> life that's put at risk with that attitude. ||||reg||13
Z||000007||Shaun41178||10-02-2000||04:25 PM||||Hey sillohuete what mods you got done to your fiero?  3.4?<P>I have also killed an 89 Vette.  I dont think I have posted this here but I will now. <P> I was out looking for trouble with my bottle open and I passed a corvette coming off a sidestreet so I gave him a bit of pipe.  He turned my way but got in a turn lane at the light I caught and I was in the straight lane.  I said "f" it and pulled out and got behind him the turn lane.  I figured I would need to be aggressive if I wanted to race.  So I turn with him and its just us two for like 2 miles.  I am giving it gas and jumping him but he won't bite.  I see the light turn red up ahead and I am in the curb lane and I am just hoping this guy won't turn left on me.  Well he doesn't and I stop right next to him and give him a rev.  He looks over and I point ahead and he nods his head yes.  He asked me what year I had and I said 85 and he said he had an 89.  He wanted to know how much hp I had and I said I had a few dollars in it.  Light turns green and I get the holeshot on this guy.  I dont know if he wasnt paying attention or what but I got a quick car before second and then pulled about another 2 cars on him up till 3rd gear in my auto tranny and then it stayed that way up till about 85 when I shut it down.  I braked and he came flying by me.  I caught up to him at the next light and we gave each other thumbs up.<P>Oh yea this was with my 2.8 and not my 3.2 as my 3.2 is not in yet.<P>I have beat numerous other cars as well.  A brand new 99 Trans Am up till 50 before we had to shut down.  I had like 3 cars on this guy too cause he spum them so bad.  I have also beaten an 89 supra turbo with fart pipe and BOV on a roll from 45-85 by about 2 cars or so.<P>I have also beaten numerous of unsuspecting Mustangs.  Too many to count and even a Grand National once.<P>You want to read some of my kills I have some of them posted on my website or you could do a general search of my handle name(shaun41178) and they should come up there too.<P>------------------<BR>Shaun-Toledo OH, 85 GT<BR>3.2 With nitrous<BR>http://members.aol.com/shaun41178||||reg||1
Z||000008||watdge||10-02-2000||04:30 PM||||Alrighty, since I see which this direction this thread is going.. how about best kill on the dragstrip or controlled race track?  None of that road stuff unless you feel inclinded to do so.<P>------------------<BR>The young, Mechanical Engineering student,<BR>Jeremy<BR> <IMG SRC="http://venus.spaceports.com/~flagg/pictureforformum.jpg"> ||||reg||3
Z||000009||Sillhouette.com||10-02-2000||05:22 PM||||Sorry Patrick about not sitting around the campfire and sing cumbaya.  Once again if you don't like my attitude there is always professional help.  It is sad however that most people that say not to street race have done it in their earlier years so they are about as bad as me.  <P>Well here goes the engine mod.....<BR>2.8 fiero engine bored out 2.9 custom pistons and shaved heads don't know how much.  Roller rockers a mild crane cam, dynamically balanced bottom end.  Port and polished intake runners and larger throttle body.  Stock exhaust manifold with stainless steel pipes larger flow cat and mufflers.  Took out the stock airbox and installed an RSM supercharger kit.  Rebuilt monzie transmission.   Those are the mods for my car.<P>Now let's talk about SOLO races.  I'm part of TLMC club mostly race by Molson Indy in Barrie.  There I've beaten most everything.  A yellow fiero was there as well with a V8 carburated very impressive acceleration moderately impressive in corners and it stalls sometimes especially if it Idles for long.  Some other cars in the club would be Civics (no challange) Integra (no challange) there is one CRX that I still have to beat.  There is also a Miata that is driven by a race car driver don't know his name.  Noone can touch the guy and what gets me is that his miata is bone stock.  <BR>I also participate in the Corvette club races.  There I place third only beaten by two trailered heavly modified Corvettes.  I have beaten an S2000 the rest were cavaliers civics sentras.  <BR>Hoping to graduate into GT class racing where you race side by side with other competitors.  Maybe next year.  I'll have to get a roll cage and some other ammenities to the race fiero.  (not my personal one)  <P>I have only been once to the 1/4 mile track.  There I've beaten a camaro that had approximately 300HP.  Beaten the thing by 1s he did have a higher top speed though.  <P>The reason I street race and a lot of my friends do as well is to get our goverments to build us a race track in the city.  So far you have to drive an hour to two hours outside the city to find some track and when you're there it's probably booked by other people.  For some reason the Wisdom of this goverment is that it makes more sense to build an indoor ski hill than a race track.  This is the way we rebell against the powers that be.  <P>Cheers||||reg||1
Z||000010||Seanh||10-02-2000||05:41 PM||||I have beat an 89 vett. He had a bored out 405 S/C engine. He just got the car, and always wanted to race me before he even knew what car he was going to get. It was on a country road about 4 miles south of town here. It was by no means a straight course. He was still learning how to drive a stick, and couldnt do it very well. I really wanted a challenge and asked him if he wanted to wait until he had some more experience with the car. Nope, he thought I was trying to get out of racing. So we went at it. We both got up to about 70 or so, he was a head of me, first turn comming up, he brakes heavy and starts sliding, I swerved off the side and got infront of him and took that corner at about 65 and slid sidways for a while, But I do know how to do some High performance driving, so it really wasnt much. He finally got up to me again and thought he was going to beat me at the last turn he took way to fast, probally 90 slid out and hit a fence post sideways. Trying to get out of the ditch and back on the road, his engine threw a rod. Hes still pissed at me, but I tried to give him a chance to wait. He still wont ever race me again now, he auctually thinks I could beat him all the time.<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8<BR>Killer Stereo System||||reg||1
Z||000011||Patrick||10-02-2000||07:02 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Once again if you don't like my attitude there is always professional help.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE> You, my friend, will be the one possibly requiring <I>professional help</I> if you kill some little kid crossing the street. Hell, at high speeds it's pretty easy to mount the curb and wipe out innocent people just walking on the sidewalk minding their own business. But it sounds like you have life all figured out. Carry on... have fun.||||reg||13
Z||000012||Fiero5||10-02-2000||08:54 PM||||Hmmm, some of you have "killed" a few Vettes, huh? That is starting to seem pretty common for most Fiero-ites by now it seems? How about this one people. On the way home yesterday from the Stratham NH car show, Tarrah and I are tooling right along in good ole' Fiero5, when as we are about 3 miles to the turn to 89 North I see up ahead what looks like a red Del Sol or something. Then I see it a bit better and it's really W-I-D-E .<BR>I ask Tarrah to hand me the DV Camcorder as it has a mean zoom on it. I power her up and while rumbling along at about 85MPH, I check out the LCD screen that conveniently pops out of the side. I zzzzoooom in on that car, and Damn! It's a Viper!<BR>Tarrah says "Dad, can you catch it?" Hmmm, I don't know I think. Awe, what the heck! "Tarrah, let's try". We make the turn onto 89 North, and I make my move. My pedal goes down a bit more and we are now going around a few cars that are in the way. I am now slowly coming up on the red Viper, and with a 4 banger and my daughter in the car I am being very carefull. I finally catch up to it after a few miles and the guy obviously see's me creeping up as he steps down on his gas pedal a bit and starts to pull away. I pick up more speed and I am able to catch up to it again. He then makes a move to the right lane and we continue to make up ground on the Viper. A few more miles and I am finally right beside it and the lady riding with him waves to Tarrah. I step on it a bit more and finally pull away and after a bit I have him in my rear view. <BR>Now, you are all saying sarcastically, "Yeah-Right!" Guess what? Remember That DV camcorder? I filmed the whole thing!!!<BR>Copies of the video are available folks!<BR>Which includes shots of the Stratham NH show too!<BR>4 Bangers rule!||||reg||1
Z||000013||watdge||10-02-2000||10:05 PM||||How much did you say those vids were running?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Would love to have a glance of it!  Nice kill  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>The young, Mechanical Engineering student,<BR>Jeremy<BR> <IMG SRC="http://venus.spaceports.com/~flagg/pictureforformum.jpg"> ||||reg||12
Z||000014||hugh||10-02-2000||10:30 PM||||I have read and reread these posts,I don't know wether to be mad at or feel sorry for these people who are proud of their street racing.I street raced when I was a KID.Only our cars were only capable of about 65mph in the 1/4 mile and I lived in a rural area with very little traffic and there were a lot fewer cars on the road. Sillhouette;I'm glad for two things;one--That I don't live near you,because I value my life and those of my kids.Two--You may develope an interest in guns and want to force the government to build an indoor range by taking pot shots at people to prove your point.After all that is what you're doing with your car.What about the tracks you raced at?  ||||reg||1
Z||000015||Sleeper||10-02-2000||10:31 PM||||What most of these Fiero Fantics are saying is they just put bigger motors in for show and cuz they gotta lotta $$$.<P>"Uhh, I gotta (V8, 3.8, 3.4, turbo, NOS, etc.) in my fiero, but I don't race."<P>I see ppl hide behind poor excuses like..."I'm gonna hurt or kill somebody if I race on the street."(so race on a Blvd and not on a residental street)..."Fieros not ment to be drag raced, so I'm not going to race in on the track."(either are hondas but the got them running 9's)...(and oh, heres the biggest B.S.)"Fieros are gunna be worth alotta money in the future, so I'm not gunna race it."(It's a sportscar, it's ment to be driven into the ground)<P>Either you don't got the guts to take your car to the limits in a race or canyon run or you just wanna show off your car.<P>Sorry guys but my 2 cents.<BR>||||reg||8
Z||000016||hugh||10-02-2000||10:54 PM||||Sleeper,Any time you are around the Philadelphia area let me know.We can go to Atco raceway and take our cars to the limit.You see,I'm not thoughtless enough to endanger other people.And when I get done blowing your doors off we can go get a beer(if you are old enough to drink).Oh,by the way,are the hondas running nines on the street?||||reg||1
Z||000017||Sillhouette.com||10-02-2000||11:12 PM||||Hugh you are what we young people call hyporcrite.  Your analogy of having less cars in the past is Antiquated as it is False.  Ask your self this how many people die each day that do not street race.  How many people return from cottage that don't know the abilities of an SUV and crush their families into small pieces.  How many people talk on the cell phone and forgett to drive.  How many people do the old rubber necking.  How many people do not use the left lane for what it was built? Passing.  How is it that on the Autobahn the speed limit is 150KPH not enforced and they have very few accidents.  Before you blame the driver schools remember who ran those things.  We are still younge who taught us how to drive if not the baby boomer generation that was street racing when there were fewer cars.  Just a few points for you to mull over.  <P>Cheers||||reg||1
Z||000018||hugh||10-02-2000||11:34 PM||||Sillhouette,Are you trying to say that there were as many cars on the road in 1957/58 as there are today?I taught all five of my kids to drive safely,not to race on the street(and they don't)Who said anything about driving schools?Nothing you said in your last post had any thing to do with what I said in mine.Did your parents teach you how to street race?Or did they teach you how to drive and then you just got stupid?When someone calls me a hypocrite and doesn't know what it means it doesn't mean much.Have a nice day.||||reg||1
Z||000019||Sillhouette.com||10-02-2000||11:39 PM||||Well let me put the word Hypocrite in simple terms.  It's a person YOU who has done the exact same thing that he is dissagreing with.  Meaning You did street racing however you wish to comfort yourself (less cars we only did 65 mph ) is irrelevant you did street racing.  Now you condemn street racers for doing something that you did as well.  So infact you're condeming yourself.  ||||reg||1
Z||000020||GT Bastard||10-02-2000||11:39 PM||||Jeezus everybody, quit bitching at each other.  The man asked about racing, not the philiosophical and moral implications of rocket science.  <P>I'm not exactly hard-core, but I enjoy the occasional race under the right circumstances.  <P>Kills to date(in the past couple months since I've had this car) include: '86 Fiero GT with a 3.1 V6 and a 4sp, '86 SE 3.1 w/4sp, ANOTHER '86 SE V6 4sp w/ a 2.8, '98 Z28 w/6sp LS1 ONLY THROUGH A LIGHT, '91 Formula 350 automatic ONLY THROUGH A LIGHT, misc riceboys and a few other 3rd gen f-bodys. <P>------------------<BR>Gold 86 SE V6 4-sp w/4.10 gears, Eibach springs, Koni's all around w/some poly bushings<BR>Yoko's<BR>Coated headers<BR>ACT 4-puck clutch<BR>MSD ignition<BR>Flowmaster w/ mandrel bent 2.5 pipe<BR>extrude honed intake<BR>Lots of fuel system mods... etc etc...||||reg||1
Z||000021||Sillhouette.com||10-02-2000||11:43 PM||||Hey GT Bastard you're right we should not phylosphise about the moral correctnes of street racing.  I'm sorry about that.<P>I do have a question what type of Fuel mods do you have?  The only one I know of is bigger injectors and high volume fuel pump. Are there any other ones out there.  <P>Later||||reg||1
Z||000022||hugh||10-02-2000||11:51 PM||||I said I was a KID.I grew up,maybe you should to.Have a nice day.||||reg||1
Z||000023||stimpy||10-02-2000||11:58 PM||||Don't know bout that one... back in the sixties people did a lot of drugs and had lots of "free" sex.Would that make someone a hypocrite now for encouraging safe sex and telling people not to smoke crack?  A bad idea is a bad idea, doesn't matter if it was done before. <P>That being said, I must admit to enjoying a little stoplight grand prix now and then, however pushing a car to 10/10ths on the street is irresponsible. It's all fun and games til someone gets hurt.<P>As for those intrepid souls who feel that they are only putting themselves at risk, let me tell ya about Nick Isom.  The Isoms were friends of our family as I was growing up. Nick always had some bad-ass rides... a 66 Nova SS, a 69 Camaro, then a Nissan minitruck that was the shotruck for California StepSides.  It was in the truck that Nick was racing  when he had to take evasive action to avoid hitting a car coming in from a side street.  Although he didn't kill anyone, he also didn't get himself killed. That might have been a blesing for him. Instead, he sustained seve brain damage, spent the rest of his life in a wheelchair and in diapers.  His parents had to take care of him for the rest of his life. This happened when he was about 19...<P>Yeah, performance cars are a lot of fun. But they are also potential weapons. Just like y'alls beloved handguns, they need to be used reponsibly with some thought as to the consequences.<P>And Patrick, why are you letting Hugh take all the crap? Get in there a slug it out... two Canadians fighting, we'll have us a hockey game!  ||||reg||1
Z||000024||Cooter||10-03-2000||12:14 AM||||I did not mean to start an international incident over racing! It seems like human nature to try to out do the next guy. I don't actively seek out a race, but when the opportunity presents itself- I (as will most anyone else) will quickly accelerate from a redlight. My car is pretty quick -3.4/4.10's four speed. But the entire idea behind building this demon was as a "commuter car". Isn't that what Pontiac sold them as back in 84? My daily drive to/from work is several miles of stop and go in town traffic. I wanted a car capable of getting me there and back safely, economically, and with a little more style than my Civic has. The extra passing power is very nice when the soccer mom in her SUV won't give up the left lane and you only have a little room and even less time to get around her. I did not build a race car, but instead it turned out to be a car I can race and have fun with.||||reg||1
Z||000025||Fiero5||10-03-2000||08:26 AM||||"How much did you say those vids were running?  Would love to have a glance of it! Nice kill" <P>Thanks. The videos would be just the cost of the tape and shipping. Say $3.00 for the VHS tape, and $5.00 for shipping I guess. Send it to:<BR>Steve Kelley<BR>POB 117<BR>Plainfield, NH 03781<P>------------------<BR>                                                          <IMG SRC="http://www.kelleyfamilyfieros.homestead.com/files/Sfiero5.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000026||Patrick||10-03-2000||04:57 PM||||<BR>Geez Stimpy, I can't be monitoring this forum 24 hours a day. Besides, Hugh's a big boy and he's been handling the "crap" just fine.<P>There are often posts here by various members who talk about their "kills". I don't usually get involved in these threads, but occasionally I feel the need to speak up. The last time I did was with someone named Voyd. That proved to be an interesting exchange, as some of our forum members may recall. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <P>It's downright scary to come across a post such as the one by Sillhouette, where right off the bat he's in our faces. Look at the first paragraph of his first post:    <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Well I got a lead foot I guess a couple of them. Life is too short to worry about carefullness and life insurance and I do race my Fiero both on the Track and on the street. If the Forum does not like that well I also know of a good psychologist that can help you get over it.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE>I agree with Hugh, I'm also grateful that I don't live near this guy. If he drives anywhere near as irresponsibly as he talks he shouldn't be allowed to get behind the wheel.<P>Shaun is well known here for his street-racing tales, and I have to admit, I enjoy reading them. Not because I agree with what he does, but because his posts are usually well written. His stories remind me of the times 25 years ago when <B><I>I</I></B> used to street-race my big block Chevys. Yes, I used to street-race myself. Not very often, but I used to do it. Several factors contributed to me no longer racing on the street, not the least of which was the fact that I grew up. It's amazing how a bit of maturity allows a person to view their actions with more of a sense of responsibility. As we get older we (usually) realize that our actions can have consequences far beyond the limits of our immediate comprehension. Stimpy's last post contains a chilling example of this. <P>It is NOT being a hypocrite to try and prevent someone from duplicating the mistakes we ourselves did in the past. Even if our comments have no effect on the person they're directed at, it's possible that at least some other individual will benefit from our efforts. That's what makes all this hassle worthwhile.<p>[This message has been edited by Patrick (edited 10-03-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000027||Seanh||10-03-2000||05:38 PM||||I dont race alot. When we do its usally out of town. I enjoy steping on it at a light and wasting that annoying neon, but its not racing, it simply accelerating fast. I never get more then 5 mph above the speed limit. I agree that you should not race on populated streets. But I think its just fine to take the cars out of town and race all night on these streets that no one ever uses. I figure, I go out in public everyday, I walk to my car, go to the mailbox, I am taking a risk because somone else is having fun. I really dont think it is too much to ask that somome else take a risk once in a great while so that I can have a little fun. Im not trying to sound selfish or anything.<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8<BR>Killer Stereo System||||reg||1
Z||000028||BBBAD GT||10-03-2000||06:11 PM||||Sillhouette.com:  I'm curious, what are your '300hp Camaro killing' 1/4 mi ETs/MPH?  <P>I think everybody knows my opinons on street racing....||||reg||1
Z||000029||Sillhouette.com||10-03-2000||06:22 PM||||Hey no problem  the time is 14.338s for fiero 14.672s for camaro  fiero 98.4mph 96.2mph for the camaro.  I stand corrected from my earlier post looking at the time slip I was wrong and the Fiero had a higher trap speed than the camaro.  Both cars modified by RSM the camaro had larger throttle body K&N, catback larger exhaust some perfomance wires.  The fiero had the RSM supercharger on it.  <P>Later||||reg||1
Z||000030||zeusrekning||10-03-2000||07:01 PM||||Just for the hell of it i'll post. I'm young and really cant afford a ticket so i drive pretty slow. i still screw up and drive agrressively once in a while. I'd rather race on the track. good luck if you do.||||reg||1
Z||000031||BBBAD GT||10-04-2000||05:51 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Sillhouette.com:<BR><B>Hey no problem  the time is 14.338s for fiero 14.672s for camaro  fiero 98.4mph 96.2mph for the camaro.  I stand corrected from my earlier post looking at the time slip I was wrong and the Fiero had a higher trap speed than the camaro.  Both cars modified by RSM the camaro had larger throttle body K&N, catback larger exhaust some perfomance wires.  The fiero had the RSM supercharger on it.  <P>Later</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Thats interesting, because the calculated HP the camaro is making based on MPH at est 3400lb is only 235hp.  Your Fiero calculates at 215hp based on est 2900lb.  I think you said your car turned about 200 rwhp. Its the camaro that I can't figure out.  If it truely had 300hp, then his weight should be 4300lb to run only 96mph.  Something is wrong with that camaro.  <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000032||KRMFiero||10-04-2000||06:30 PM||||Just wondering.... I have a 84 Fiero 2M4 SE with a automatic transmition,  this is will be my first  car, it will be on the road in like 2 months and i have never drove it.... I'm just wondering  can this car spin out? do brak stands or anything to get some smoke from the tiers?   My sister has a 86 Ford Escort, It can spin the tiers 1st, 2nd and sometiems chearp 3rd  lol its pretty funny but it is a standard and the way she does it there will be no clutch in about another month heheh well anyways, anyone got a pic of any Fiero Spinning out? thanx||||reg||5
Z||000033||Sillhouette.com||10-04-2000||09:19 PM||||Yep you are right something is wrong with the camaro.  He could not hook up.  That is where I won.  My tires never chirped the hookup was perfect.  He spun the tires until about quarter track than he hooked up and stayed just a bit behind me all the way down the track.  The camaro is a 1996 six speed 5.7 L engine.  Since the race a set of headers have been installed on the camaro. That should lower his torque figures so probably his hookup would be much better now.  Coincidently that was the problem with the race fiero as well.  The tires did not hook up even in third gear.  <BR>The race fiero is a 1985GT stripped completley about 1900LBS as is with racing slicks (BF Goodrich R1) and a 2.9 V6 with roller rockers shaved heads custom pistons balanced bottom end larger intake throttle body exhaust and no cat just straight through.  The engine was hooked up to a four speed tranny.  No supercharger yet.  <BR>I wish I could give you the 1/8 numbers but the slip is torn and very light I can't make out the numbers.  <BR>Hope this explains it a bit better. <P>Later||||reg||1
Z||000034||88formula||10-04-2000||09:20 PM||||No||||reg||1
Z||000035||BBBAD GT||10-05-2000||09:23 AM||||Hmmmmm, it looks like the driver of the Camaro has never been to the strip before, spinning all the way to quarter track.  If he just backed off a little until it did hook, then pour it on as the chassis would allow, the ET's would of been better.  I don't think headers will kill his torque enough for him to hook, in contrary, it should increase his torque across the board and he'll have a more difficult time hooking.<P>I'd make the suggestion of both the Camaro and the race Fiero to get some real drag slicks to hook.  The sidewalls of road racing slicks are alot more stiff than drag slicks, and are not prone to 'wrinkling'.  <P>My drag racing experience $.02....<P><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/BBBAD_GT_SIG.gif">    <P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/V8Fiero" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD V8</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/Fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD GT</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD 5.0</A>||||reg||1
