Z||000041||hugh||10-05-2000||10:05 PM||||Sleeper,<BR>I live about 7 miles from Atco raceway.It's a 1/4 mile track.Every year they have a Pan Am meet.There are 4 cylinder cars and dragsters that are unbelieveable.Nine seconds is very fast but nothing extraordinary.My family car is not a race car.It weighs about 3700 lbs. with me in it,and has a 231 cubic inch engine,It gets over 20 mpg on the highway and about 15 mpg around town,has air, cruise,pw,ps,pb,seats five,and is comfortable.It also has run 115mph@12.20 in the 1/4.With it's current settup it should run around11.5@117/118.I think it is fair to say It is a relatively fast car.I don't race it on the street.I don't have anything to prove. The post by Old Lar isn't to prove anything,just to show how catastrophic an accident can be.||||reg||1
