Z||000044||Cheever2||10-06-2000||01:57 AM||||Holy cow, I been away one week, took a long time to catch up on this one.  But I've been thinking about it all week, and WATDGE you asked a reasonable question: you wanted to hear stories.  And some of us jumped all over you about it.  Well I remember my share of street races in my teens, and then I got into 4-wheelers, sandbuggies & baja bugs.  I definitely recommend the offroad stuff if you like to get a little crazy and if you like to hear your engine revving.  But I apologize for forgetting that people DO race on the street, as I certainly did.  So I shoulda stayed out of it and let people tell their stories.  I just changed, and I like Fieros out of appreciation for the cars sorta like works of art, not for what they can (or can't) do.  Anyway, welcome to the Forum.  You'll read more kill stories as you hang around.  If you go racing past me, I'll just watch, thank you very much.||||reg||1
